Subject: Report which kind of C++ method a function is

bindgen renders a C++ method as a free function whose name is built from the
class's name and the method's, so the generated Rust says nothing about which
methods are constructors. `ParseCallbacks::denote_special_member` covers only
the special members, which leaves a constructor taking arguments of its own
indistinguishable from any other method - a consumer that emits C++ has to
guess from the name, and `Widget::Widget3()` guesses wrong.

bindgen already has the answer in `ir::comp::MethodKind`, computed from the
cursor at parse time. Make that enum public and add an additive
`ParseCallbacks::denote_method_kind`, reported from function codegen beside the
existing item facts.

